  "claim": "The Day After, a 1982 film that aired in 1983, was the seventh highest rated non-sports show and featured a Kansas state highway. The De Soto High School (Kansas) is located off this highway.",
  "evidencia": "Page: K-10 (Kansas highway). Sentence: K-10 is a 38-mile (61 km) state highway in the U.S. state of Kansas.\nPage: K-10 (Kansas highway). Sentence: Several scenes for the TV-movie \"The Day After\" were filmed on the highway in 1982 portraying a mass exodus evacuating the Kansas City area on I-70.\nPage: The Day After. Sentence: The Day After is an American television film that first aired on November 20, 1983, on the ABC television network.\nPage: The Day After. Sentence: With a 46 rating and a 62% share of the viewing audience during its initial broadcast, it was the seventh highest rated non-sports show up to that time and set a record as the highest-rated television film in history—a record it still held as recently as a 2009 report.\nPage: De Soto High School (Kansas). Sentence: The school is located off of K-10 and Lexington Avenue on 91st street.",
