        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kansas, Kansas City area, De Soto High School\n- Systems: K-10, I-70\n- Products: The Day After\n- Organizations: ABC television network\n\nFacts:\n- K-10 is a 38-mile state highway in Kansas.\n- In 1982, several scenes for The Day After were filmed on K-10 to portray a mass exodus evacuating the Kansas City area on I-70.\n- The Day After first aired on November 20, 1983, on the ABC television network.\n- During its initial broadcast, The Day After earned a 46 rating and a 62% audience share.\n- The Day After became the seventh highest-rated non-sports show up to that time and set the record for the highest-rated television film in history, which it still held as recently as a 2009 report.\n- De Soto High School is located off K-10 and Lexington Avenue on 91st Street.",
